# FluidRendererImpl Call Walkthrough

Keep this page in the Fabric rendering directory first; the entry point is `FluidRendererImpl.java`:

```text
fabric/src/main/java/net/caffeinemc/mods/sodium/fabric/render/FluidRendererImpl.java
```

The only objects visible in the file header are this group:

```java
package net.caffeinemc.mods.sodium.fabric.render;

import com.mojang.blaze3d.vertex.VertexConsumer;
import net.caffeinemc.mods.sodium.client.model.color.ColorProvider;
import net.caffeinemc.mods.sodium.client.model.color.ColorProviderRegistry;
```

At the time, `VertexConsumer` was placed on the vertex-output side, while `ColorProvider` and `ColorProviderRegistry` were placed on the color-related side. The old reading assumed that the registry would select a provider, which would then participate in fluid color processing; this relationship still has no corresponding member-access snippet. When retracing it, start with these three names in the file, first check what kinds of statements each appears in, and then decide whether to move into the color package.

# TranslucentGeometr Adapter Entry Walkthrough

This name is a search label left over from the rendering layers. Narrow the target to `common/src/main/java/net/caffeinemc/mods/sodium/client/render/chunk/translucent_sorting/TranslucentGeometryCollector.java` first. The class name is `TranslucentGeometryCollector`; the spelling in the title was not carried forward as the class name.

The file is located at `net.caffeinemc.mods.sodium.client.render.chunk.translucent_sorting`. It was initially noted as the “adapter point where translucent geometry enters the sorting side,” but that interpretation had not yet been tied to a method signature.

```java
package net.caffeinemc.mods.sodium.client.render.chunk.translucent_sorting;

import it.unimi.dsi.fastutil.objects.ReferenceArrayList;
import net.caffeinemc.mods.sodium.api.util.NormI8;
import net.caffeinemc.mods.sodium.client.SodiumClientMod;
```

Start from the class name and return to these three direct dependencies: `ReferenceArrayList`, `NormI8`, and `SodiumClientMod`. This is a useful place to check which objects appear around the collector, not a basis for treating it as the complete sorting flow.

Tentative walkthrough order: top of the file → class construction and public methods → locations where `NormI8` appears → connections to `SodiumClientMod`. TODO: add method-level notes; confirm whether “adapter entry” is just an old navigation label.
